      "text": "I went to a bakery this morning, about a 10 minute walk away, that had local sweets that are only found in the Kathmandu valley. The Sel Roti you can find across Nepal, but another treat was a crispy Kakhamari (or Jalebi) wih chaku (sugarcane wheat paste) wrapped in a flexible thin pita thing.",
